WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:03.370
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here!

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:08.140
As you know, I absolutely loved Zootopia,
and each time I watch the movie, I find something

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.140
new to enjoy.

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:13.150
But because of the way animated movies are
made, there's often tons of incredible stuff

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:16.510
that the animators work on which doesn't make
it into the final movie.

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:20.529
So, in this video, I'm going to be taking
a look at the dozens of amazing deleted scenes

00:00:20.529 --> 00:00:24.160
and rejected ideas from Zootopia that hit
the cutting room floor.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:28.220
And a quick warning that of course there are
spoilers ahead, so if you want to avoid any

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:32.850
spoilers, click here for my spoiler-free review
or come back after you've seen the movie.

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:38.020
Just before I get started I've got another
fantastic copy of this gorgeous hardback book

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:39.800
The Art of Zootropolis to give away.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:44.460
All you have to do is subscribe and leave
a comment about the deleted scenes on this

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:45.460
video.

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:49.170
To give you an idea of what you can look forward
to in the book, there's tons of amazing concept

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:54.170
art, sketches, and information that give an
incredible peek into the making of the movie.

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:59.829
First up is the movie's opening scene which
sets Judy up to become a police officer in

00:00:59.829 --> 00:01:03.270
Zootopia although in a different way than
we see in the final movie.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:07.090
The alternate opening is set in Woodlands
Elementary School rather than at the Carrot

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:12.170
Days Festival and has Judy practising a song
with her classmates while their teacher Mrs

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:14.350
Armadillo accompanies them on the piano.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:17.940
Judy's friends each sing a line about what
they want to be when they grow up, but when

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:21.479
it comes to Judy's turn, she won't sing that
she wants to grow carrots.

00:01:21.479 --> 00:01:26.579
This opening establishes how animals are stereotyped,
for example, Sally the squirrel sings that

00:01:26.579 --> 00:01:30.959
she wants to sell nuts and the Rory the racoon
sings that he wants to drive a trash truck.

00:01:30.959 --> 00:01:35.619
But Judy proves she's capable of other things
when Bobby Catmull the cougar cub is about

00:01:35.619 --> 00:01:37.340
to fall out of a tree.

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:41.649
Judy grabs Mrs Armadillo's laser pen and gets
Bobby to chase its light down the tree to

00:01:41.649 --> 00:01:42.649
safety.

00:01:42.649 --> 00:01:47.189
A police offer then arrives and gives Judy
a Junior ZPD badge and says she should become

00:01:47.189 --> 00:01:48.630
a police officer.

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:53.669
And when Judy's classmate scoffs that she's
just a bunny, the officer replies "This is

00:01:53.669 --> 00:01:57.939
Zootopia where anyone can be anything", a
moment which echoes what Judy does and says

00:01:57.939 --> 00:02:00.060
to Finnick later in the final movie.

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:04.239
Other elements from this alternate opening
scene also appeared in a slightly different

00:02:04.239 --> 00:02:05.899
form in the final movie.

00:02:05.899 --> 00:02:10.709
Bobby Catmull appears as the cougar who creates
the various sound effects during Judy's performance

00:02:10.709 --> 00:02:16.220
at Carrot Days and Mrs Armadillo is the landlady
at Judy's apartment complex.

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:20.780
And the scene in the alternate opening which
features a deer being mock-attacked by a predator

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:25.280
as part of the rehearsals for the school's
show mirrors both the dramatic scene Judy

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:30.319
performs with fake blood in the opening of
the final movie and also the final movie's

00:02:30.319 --> 00:02:36.950
climactic showdown when Nick fakes turning
savage to catch Bellwether.

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:41.680
Since Zootopia came out, there've been tons
of fans shipping Judy and Nick, and an incredible

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:44.209
amount of fan art on just that subject.

00:02:44.209 --> 00:02:47.940
So, shippers of Nick and Judy everywhere will
likely love this next deleted scene I'm going

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:48.940
to talk about which features Nick meeting
Judy's parents and her dad assuming that Nick

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:49.940
is Judy's boyfriend!

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:52.939
The scene would have appeared in the movie
just after everyone's favourite fox and bunny

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:55.950
team escape Manchas who's gone savage.

00:02:55.950 --> 00:03:00.459
In the scene, Judy and Nick arrive at her
very pink apartment which prompts Nick to

00:03:00.459 --> 00:03:04.299
question Judy's description of where they
were going as a 'safe-house'.

00:03:04.299 --> 00:03:09.370
Judy's reply that it's a 'safe house, with
a space in the middle, a house that is safe'

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:14.370
is a fantastic riff on Nick's earlier words
to Judy that he was not falsely advertising

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:19.659
the Redwood he sold the rodents as it was
actually 'red wood with a space in the middle,

00:03:19.659 --> 00:03:21.400
wood that is red'.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:25.170
Judy's family have come to the big city to
pay her a surprise visit, and when Judy's

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:30.299
father first sees Nick, he asks her to pass
him the fox-taser, and then worries that Nick

00:03:30.299 --> 00:03:32.219
is her boyfriend.

00:03:32.219 --> 00:03:37.739
The family also discovers that Judy is a meter
maid, not a real cop as she'd led them to

00:03:37.739 --> 00:03:42.859
believe, so her father demands that she leave
Zootopia and return home with them, but Nick

00:03:42.859 --> 00:03:44.530
steps in to defend her.

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:48.689
In the final movie, this moment was replaced
with Chief Bogo rather than her father trying

00:03:48.689 --> 00:03:50.920
to make Judy leave the police force.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:56.950
There are some really amazing designs for
Judy's family home in Bunnyburrow that didn't

00:03:56.950 --> 00:03:58.700
make it to the final movie.

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:02.810
The huge size of Judy's family and house was
going to be a major feature of the film with

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:06.200
over 200 bunnies running around.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:09.909
In fact, originally, Judy's family was so
large that her father couldn't even remember

00:04:09.909 --> 00:04:10.909
her name!

00:04:10.909 --> 00:04:15.489
Also, the family home was going to be centred
around a constantly-in-use kitchen and a dining

00:04:15.489 --> 00:04:20.280
area that rotated slowly allowing new hungry
bunnies to take the place of bunnies who'd

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:22.330
already finished eating.

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:26.720
And The Bunnyburrow district was also going
to feature more of the Totoro-inspired buildings

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:32.750
we only saw briefly in the final film at the
Bunnyburrow train station.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:36.370
During the chase through Little Rodentia,
you might have spotted a billboard for the

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:38.810
fast food restaurant Chez Cheese.

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:42.580
In an early draft of the movie, Finnick would
take the drive-thru orders making use of his

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:46.800
giant ears while Nick worked cleaning the
cheese filters.

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:51.150
In that version of the movie, Clawhauser was
also a delivery cheetah for the restaurant,

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:53.389
making deliveries to the district's rodents.

00:04:53.389 --> 00:04:56.900
Chez Cheese was going to tell the story of
how Nick and Finnick met.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:05:00.979
The movie's co-director Jared Bush has said
this was his favourite deleted location and

00:05:00.979 --> 00:05:06.389
that he'd love to see a short film featuring
the fast food joint.

00:05:06.389 --> 00:05:11.310
Another fast food joint which didn't appear
was Bug-Burga which is where Zootopia's predators

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:12.590
would go to eat.

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:16.650
Because predators don't eat other animals
in Zootopia, to get their protein they eat

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:22.180
insects, so Bug-Burga served up "grasshopper
shakes, cricket chips and cicada burgers."

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:26.400
There is a tiny reference to Bug-Burga in
the final film in the scene where Nick is

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:30.639
leading Judy through an alleyway shortcut
and there are some Bug-Burga fast food boxes

00:05:30.639 --> 00:05:32.350
littered on the ground.

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:37.800
Originally, there was going to be more of
Nick's backstory explored in the film, including

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:40.800
a scene where we get to see Nick as a cub
with his father.

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:44.880
It's a touching moment where Nick's father
goes with his son to pitch a business idea

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:49.449
for a loan so he can start his own family
tailoring shop called Suit-topia.

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:53.669
The scene wasn't used as it was part of the
initial idea for the film where the story

00:05:53.669 --> 00:05:58.569
was told from Nick's perspective as the central
character, rather than through Judy's eyes.

00:05:58.569 --> 00:06:04.599
We know Nick has always had an entrepreneurial
mind with his pawpsicle business, but in an

00:06:04.599 --> 00:06:08.590
early version of Zootopia, just like his father,
Nick went to the Zootopian banks to pitch

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:13.310
a business idea, but Nick's idea was for an
entertainment venue called Wild Times.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:19.540
In a scene which was actually voiced by Jason
Bateman, Nick explained his idea to all of

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:22.319
the city's bankers, who just happened to all
be prey.

00:06:22.319 --> 00:06:28.389
It's a funny scene where Nick visits banks
like Lemming Brothers, Borrow Burrow, JP Mare-Gan

00:06:28.389 --> 00:06:31.880
and Slothoman Brothers, and gets rejected
every time.

00:06:31.880 --> 00:06:36.650
Eventually, Nick ends up visiting the polar
bear gangster boss Koslov who loans him the

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:37.889
money.

00:06:37.889 --> 00:06:41.699
The designs for Wild Times were well-advanced
before the idea was abandoned.

00:06:41.699 --> 00:06:46.300
Wild Times was an indoor arcade where predators
could let their instincts loose a little.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:49.699
The amusement park featured a huge range of
games and rides.

00:06:49.699 --> 00:06:54.240
For example, there was a roller coaster called
the Roar-A-Coaster where predators could roar

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:55.669
and be themselves.

00:06:55.669 --> 00:06:59.629
By the way, there's a glimpse of what might
have been the building for Wild Times in the

00:06:59.629 --> 00:07:03.730
scene where Judy goes to find Nick by the
small stone bridge.

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:10.300
Koslov, who Nick takes a loan from to finance
his Wild Times arcade, did appear in the final

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:13.930
movie as the polar bear who carries Mr Big
in his hands when Nick and Judy have been

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:16.030
caught by Kevin and Raymond.

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:20.910
In earlier versions though, he ran the mafia
in Tundra Town and he owned a restaurant called

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:24.990
Koslov's Palace which served as a front for
his shady operations.

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:29.879
The design of the interior of Koslov's Palace
used warm colours to contrast with the icy

00:07:29.879 --> 00:07:34.169
blue and white of the cold exterior.

00:07:34.169 --> 00:07:38.139
The scene we see in the final movie of Nick
and Finnick hustling Judy into paying for

00:07:38.139 --> 00:07:42.569
their Jumbo Pop is a much revised version
from an earlier version of the movie.

00:07:42.569 --> 00:07:47.289
That early alternate scene in Jumbeaux's Café
shows Nick claiming that his son has a condition

00:07:47.289 --> 00:07:51.350
called "pachydermiopathy", which according
to Nick means that his son thinks he's an

00:07:51.350 --> 00:07:52.350
elephant.

00:07:52.350 --> 00:07:56.520
Nick and Finnick put on a hilarious performance
with Nick begging the ice cream parlour owner

00:07:56.520 --> 00:08:01.350
not to break his son's heart when he refuses
to serve him what he wants, and then to cap

00:08:01.350 --> 00:08:04.340
it all Nick claims he left his wallet at the
orphanage.

00:08:04.340 --> 00:08:09.500
Nick senses Judy's fallen for his scheme,
so lays the sob story on even further, which

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:12.460
ends in Judy pulling out her cash to pay.

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:16.430
It's still very funny as it displays Nick
and Finnick's con-man skills although Judy

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:19.379
probably comes off a bit more naïve and silly
in this version.

00:08:19.379 --> 00:08:26.640
In the final movie, after Judy discovers she
was hustled by Nick, she goes back to her

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:30.520
apartment feeling really fed up, and gets
a call from her parents who discover she's

00:08:30.520 --> 00:08:31.520
just a meter maid.

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:35.400
There's an earlier and longer version of this
scene where we see Judy travel back to the

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:39.310
apartment on the subway, getting squashed
by two larger animals.

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:44.340
In this version, after discarding her microwaved
carrots for one, she goes to call her mum,

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:45.450
but stops herself.

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:49.640
However, the phone accidentally dials and
she ends up talking to her parents and her

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:52.820
grandfather who's very prejudiced against
foxes.

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:57.960
In this version, her parents don't realise
she's just a meter maid which makes Judy feel

00:08:57.960 --> 00:09:00.040
guilty for hiding the truth from them.

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:04.260
It's a much sadder version of the scene than
the one in the movie and ends with Judy curling

00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:06.760
up on her bed among her cuddly toys.

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:10.690
By the way, Judy's grandfather "Pop-Pop" is
the rabbit we see at the train station in

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:15.420
the final movie, the one who bears a very
close resemblance to Carl from Up.

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:20.370
There's a deleted scene in which Judy starts
her investigation into the missing otter,

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:24.710
Emmet Otterton, by using the office and computer
of an elephant cop who's away on vacation.

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:30.200
It's a fun scene where Judy has to use her
agility to use a computer that's way bigger

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:31.260
than she is.

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:35.450
The scene was edited out of the final movie
to keep the film's pace up and to show Judy

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:41.620
getting her lead on Otterton by working more
closely with Clawhauser.

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:45.290
Designs for a rough biker-style bar for sheep
were developed although the location didn't

00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:46.790
make it into the final film.

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:50.980
The bar was called The Cloven Hoof and it
was set in a sleazy part of town.

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:54.750
It's likely that we would have seen Doug and
other bad sheep like Jesse and Woolter hanging

00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:56.500
out here.

00:09:56.500 --> 00:10:02.090
The filmmakers also had plans for a Nocturnal
District, which was going to be an area of

00:10:02.090 --> 00:10:06.060
caves underneath the city where nocturnal
animals like bats would live.

00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:10.820
In the end, Zootopia's story didn't require
the location so the idea wasn't fully developed,

00:10:10.820 --> 00:10:15.650
however, it might be linked to the Bat Eyewitness
figure who appears together with Clawhauser

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:20.620
in Zootopia character packs, and who is described
as visiting Clawhauser at the police station

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:25.420
quite frequently as he often witnesses crimes.

00:10:25.420 --> 00:10:28.830
The Meadowlands is another district that we
never got to see properly.

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:33.060
It's basically a broad grassland area where
the sheep and grazing animals live.

00:10:33.060 --> 00:10:37.350
We did get a tiny peek at the edge of the
Meadowlands though, as the Cliffside Asylum

00:10:37.350 --> 00:10:39.080
was just on the border.

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:42.840
In an early draft of the movie, there was
a sheep conspiracy where sheep would disguise

00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:47.030
themselves as wolves to deliberately incriminate
predators, making them look dangerous.

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:51.000
If you'd like to find out about one of the
sheep characters, called Wooly, who used to

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:56.940
do this, then check out my video on Zootopia's
Deleted Characters.

00:10:56.940 --> 00:11:01.330
Another location that didn't make it into
the final film was Outback Island, which was

00:11:01.330 --> 00:11:06.830
home to Australian animals such as kangaroos,
koalas, platypuses and dingos, who all together

00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:08.660
were known as "Outbackers".

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:12.710
This location was cut as it didn't fit the
main story, although it does appear in the

00:11:12.710 --> 00:11:17.540
book "Zootopia: The Stinky Cheese Caper (and
Other Cases from the ZPD Files)."

00:11:17.540 --> 00:11:22.901
There was an additional scene at the Natural
History Museum which was cut from the film

00:11:22.901 --> 00:11:24.540
due to time constraints.

00:11:24.540 --> 00:11:29.150
The cut scene featured Bellwether making a
speech to Judy about the origins of Zootopia.

00:11:29.150 --> 00:11:33.470
Those origins relate back to a painting which
if you're extremely eagle-eyed you can glimpse

00:11:33.470 --> 00:11:35.900
in the museum as well as at the subway station.

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:40.310
The painting shows lions and zebras shaking
paws and agreeing to predators and prey living

00:11:40.310 --> 00:11:41.430
in peace.

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:45.230
While giving the speech in this scene, Bellwether
looks out at and talks about the fountain

00:11:45.230 --> 00:11:49.560
in the square which represents the watering
hole around which the animals bonded when

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:51.270
they declared peace.

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:57.310
Although we do get to see the Palm Hotel and
Casino on the train ride Judy takes into the

00:11:57.310 --> 00:12:02.250
city when she arrives, there were also extensive
designs and scenes storyboarded inside the

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:04.500
hotel that did not get used.

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:10.260
The design of the hotel was inspired by super-luxurious
hotels in Dubai, and Gazelle had a penthouse

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:11.812
apartment at the Palm hotel.

00:12:11.812 --> 00:12:16.060
A scene with Judy and Nick falling down the
side of the hotel while escaping from a ram

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:19.910
was storyboarded but dropped in favour of
the scene in the Rainforest District where

00:12:19.910 --> 00:12:23.900
Judy and Nick fall through the vines while
escaping from the savage Manchas.

00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:30.980
An earlier version of the movie's action-packed
finale was set in a large stadium called Zootennial

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:31.980
Stadium.

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:36.510
There was going to be a spectacular Olympic
Games-style opening show called Animalia which

00:12:36.510 --> 00:12:38.560
showcased the history of Zootopia.

00:12:38.560 --> 00:12:42.850
It was going to feature Gazelle, who's a prey
animal, performing with her predator back-up

00:12:42.850 --> 00:12:43.900
dancers.

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:47.590
And there were going to be flying squirrels
and pigs, and animals shot out of confetti

00:12:47.590 --> 00:12:48.590
cannons.

00:12:48.590 --> 00:12:53.160
And that huge show would have acted as the
backdrop for the movie's climactic showdown.

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:56.990
The film did, of course, end with Gazelle
performing with her tiger dancers at a pop

00:12:56.990 --> 00:13:00.620
concert, but that was after Judy and Nick
had already caught the baddies.

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:02.410
The final version we see in the movie was
a cool way to show off the movie's credits.

00:13:02.410 --> 00:13:05.450
So guys, do you think any of those deleted
scenes or ideas should have been in the final

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:06.450
movie?

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:08.120
And what would you like to see in a Zootopia
sequel?

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:11.920
I can't wait to hear your thoughts in the
comments below.

00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:17.240
And don't forget to subscribe and comment
for your chance to win this beautiful Art

00:13:17.240 --> 00:13:18.620
of Zootropolis hardback book.

